{"id":"case-1989c918c7946c","assertion":"A workflow is a compiled, sandboxed coordination strategy whose symbolic control flow and explicit state sequence delegated LLM calls.","follow":"B gives the select/call normal form, state requirements, and boundary conditions for checking that correspondence.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider calling the workflow the same coordination form as the prompt-driven strategy and claiming the correspondence is exact; the narrower primitive-action claim is separate.","reconsider_changed":"If B's preconditions or treatment of concurrency and external state changed, recheck A's claims for the concrete workflow and its call order.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The coordination-compilation note asserts that its workflow instantiates B's select/call program form.","confidence":"high","justification":"A names symbolic orchestration, explicit state, and repeated calls; B formalizes exactly those elements and states when the correspondence fails."}
{"id":"case-2632bc38d6c3e7","assertion":"A says an internal process may act through a methodology, but actionability alone does not establish a reflective system.","follow":"B specifies the operator, available operations, target, and setting needed before a methodology can mediate action.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's operational reading of acting through a methodology and its claim that actionability is insufficient; self-representation and causal connection would still need separate review.","reconsider_changed":"If B's operator, access, or target conditions changed or became unavailable, reassess whether a methodology can participate in A's causal path.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The reflective-system note asserts that B's actionability condition can describe use through a methodology without establishing reflection.","confidence":"high","justification":"A separates action through a representation from reflection, while B supplies situated-use conditions but not self-representation or causal connection."}
{"id":"case-f88ac900b7b30e","assertion":"A says an author should fix goals, constraints, completion criteria, and genuinely arbitrary conventions while leaving situational methods to the executor.","follow":"B states the general rule to commit low-degree-of-freedom choices first and applies it across authoring and execution roles.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's independent ordering rationale for fixing low-flexibility details first; its stale-snapshot argument would remain, but the convergence of the two reasons would weaken.","reconsider_changed":"If B's degree-of-freedom rule or workflow application changed, revise A's sequencing guidance and examples.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The executor-guidance note asserts that B's low-degree-of-freedom rule explains which commitments an author should fix early.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly derives its author-slot rule from degrees of freedom, and B states the same rule plus the delegation case."}
{"id":"case-30111db7b8e1ad","assertion":"A says machinery in a reflective loop persists only when its warrant continues to discriminate, while symbolic machinery itself can become a learning target.","follow":"B explains why symbolic scheduling and bookkeeping machinery can be treated as a revisable target through codification.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's use of scheduler separation as an example of loop-produced machinery and its claim that the symbolic layer is a justified learning target; the broader persistence thesis is not settled by B.","reconsider_changed":"If B's error-correction asymmetry or scheduler implementation changed, update A's example and its codification claims.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The machinery-persistence note asserts that B's symbolic scheduler is revisable machinery whose persistence still requires warrant.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A discusses symbolic machinery and codification as a learning target, while B explains the scheduler rationale without establishing A's governance thesis."}
{"id":"case-fa13dc1364da68","assertion":"A says an abstracted lesson is trustworthy only when its condition clause states where the generalization stops, treating that boundary as explanatory reach.","follow":"B supplies the premise-variation, transfer, and criticism tests that make the boundary clause meaningful.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's use of explanatory reach as the boundary test and its confidence in failure-derived lessons; retaining concrete instances when scope is unknown would remain defensible.","reconsider_changed":"If B's reach tests or treatment of adaptive versus explanatory information changed, update A's condition-clause rule and success/failure rationale.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The memory-abstraction note asserts that B's explanatory-reach tests specify where an abstracted lesson should stop.","confidence":"high","justification":"A names explanatory reach and prediction of failure as its discriminator; B defines the same premise-variation and transfer tests."}
{"id":"case-c3ffb8d4901349","assertion":"A says process edits can invalidate artifacts without invalidating verdicts because later review cannot see unrecorded production history.","follow":"B explains the production-time recording and re-derivability conditions behind that state/history asymmetry.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that re-review cannot detect process-side defects and that process edits require regeneration rather than re-judgment.","reconsider_changed":"If B's recording or re-derivability conditions changed, revise A's process-side invalidation and review-contract implications.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The criteria-process note asserts that B's history constraint explains why process changes can invalidate artifacts without invalidating verdicts.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's process-side example and B's state/history account both say a bounded later reviewer cannot recover unrecorded production facts."}
{"id":"case-3f238a6bfb20f0","assertion":"A says bad generated candidates are filtered by evaluation, whereas a bad acceptance becomes operative through retention.","follow":"B defines the search, evaluation, and operative-retention functions that give A's asymmetry its exact scope.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's asymmetry and its advice to automate search first, because without B's loop structure there is no defined terminal acceptance filter.","reconsider_changed":"If B changed what counts as evaluation or operative retention, revise A's error asymmetry, correction path, and automation recommendation.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The false-positive note asserts that B's proposal-selection loop makes accepted evaluation errors operative.","confidence":"high","justification":"A uses the loop's search, evaluation, and retention vocabulary, and B defines the same sequence and its failure boundary."}
{"id":"case-f2af1a1b9045ca","assertion":"A says increasing computational autonomy shifts human effort toward harder frontier judgments rather than necessarily reducing total hours.","follow":"B distinguishes computational closure from methodological closure and supplies the actor-allocation frame needed to interpret A's measurements.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that autonomy should be measured as allocation and frontier movement rather than methodological settlement; the elastic-backlog mechanism would need separate support.","reconsider_changed":"If B's closure definitions or per-function allocation frame changed, revise A's measurements and its exclusion of methodological closure.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The autonomy note asserts that B's computational-closure distinction is needed to read human effort as actor allocation rather than methodological settlement.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly separates computational allocation from methodological closure, and B defines both terms with the same measurement caution."}
{"id":"case-c299eb39a9c550","assertion":"A says theory, description, and prescription profiles are named objective-function bundles with distinct quality goals and verification regimes.","follow":"B enumerates those profiles, their priorities, maintenance behavior, and open-ended status.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claims that the bundles are proven, that the hierarchy makes objective choice cheap, and that their oracle strengths have the stated defaults.","reconsider_changed":"If B's profile definitions, quality priorities, or maintenance semantics changed, revise A's objective hierarchy and verification discussion.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The objective-function note asserts that B's three profiles are the named bundles from which its constrained objective choices are specialized.","confidence":"high","justification":"A names the same profiles and quality differences that B presents in its table and maintenance discussion."}
{"id":"case-9a724e4374e080","assertion":"A says claim titles expose commitments so maintenance can focus on claims worth challenging rather than requiring every note to be opened.","follow":"B explains that claim-level conjectures need falsifiers and that structural criticism is necessary under bounded context.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's Popperian justification and the claim that exposed titles materially lower maintenance cost; claim titles might retain a navigation benefit.","reconsider_changed":"If B's falsifier or contradiction-checking practices changed, revise A's account of how claim titles support maintenance.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The title-maintenance note asserts that B's falsifiability requirement makes exposed claim commitments useful for review.","confidence":"high","justification":"A ties claim titles to challengeability, and B distinguishes claim-level falsifiers from runtime interpretation tests."}
{"id":"case-6152a54e6a18c8","assertion":"A says the human proxy breaks when agents interpret read text as possible instruction and choose an interpretation where a human would ask for clarification.","follow":"B explains semantic underspecification and the projection from one natural-language specification to one selected program.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's final exception about confabulation and the scope of the human proxy; the access-mode distinction alone would not establish that exception.","reconsider_changed":"If B's account of underspecification, decoding, or code boundaries changed, revise A's exception and any response that assumes interpretation replaces clarification.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The first-time-human note asserts that B's underspecification phenomenon is a separate way agent behavior can diverge from human ergonomics.","confidence":"high","justification":"A expressly isolates instruction-like reading and confabulation as exceptions, and B supplies the interpretation mechanism but not the access-cost argument."}
{"id":"case-15b46d34f5e07e","assertion":"A says filesystem location is physically total while optional frontmatter type classification is partial before validation.","follow":"B states that type metadata is optional, structural, and a search aid, supplying the premise for A's contrast with physical placement.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's example of partial type assignment and its claim that location and type have different native guarantees.","reconsider_changed":"If B's type system became mandatory, closed, or differently scoped, revise A's partiality, portability, and routing conclusions.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The directory-placement note asserts that B's opt-in type system makes classification partial while filesystem location remains total.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's frontmatter example and B's free-form, optional type description match directly."}
{"id":"case-0f41b0d385292b","assertion":"A says gates, validators, and other machinery persist by warrant rather than by occupying an exempt position outside the reflective loop.","follow":"B defines warranted autonomy as unattended operation limited to the domain an oracle can assess adequately.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that governance and accumulated oracles can replace exemption by position, especially that a gate earns persistence through discrimination.","reconsider_changed":"If B's oracle-domain or warrant conditions changed, revise which machinery A may leave unattended and how governance substitutes for a fixed point.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The machinery-persistence note asserts that B's oracle-bounded warrant is the condition for revisable machinery to persist without an external fixed point.","confidence":"high","justification":"A makes warrant the persistence criterion for gates and validators, while B defines warrant as objective- and domain-relative oracle coverage."}
{"id":"case-93f1ff2073f163","assertion":"A says natural-language and symbolic artifacts form a tractable coupled target because they share the agent's finite context and the codification boundary.","follow":"B supplies the feasibility and aggregate-cost account that makes context a shared resource and explains why symbolic scheduling matters.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's choice of the readable pair as the tractable first target and its claim that context creates their strongest coupling.","reconsider_changed":"If B's scarcity, feasibility, or cost account changed materially, revise A's coupling and validation-radius argument.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The readable-artifact note asserts that B's context constraint couples natural-language and symbolic artifacts into a tractable optimization target.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly bases the pair on shared context and codification, and B makes context scarcity and symbolic scheduling central premises."}
{"id":"case-d45ce3e679afe0","assertion":"A says generated code from an underspecified natural-language prompt is a committed interpretation because the prompt does not determine the selected program.","follow":"B explains the one-to-many specification-to-program projection and separates semantic underspecification from execution indeterminism.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's generated-code example and the claim that prompt material alone cannot determine the retained program; the human commitment examples would remain.","reconsider_changed":"If B's account of underspecification, deterministic decoding, or code projection changed, revise A's generated-code treatment and its derivation boundary.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The commitment note asserts that B's underspecified prompt is projected into a committed program rather than mechanically derived code.","confidence":"high","justification":"A relies on source non-determination, and B explicitly states that natural-language specifications admit multiple programs even at temperature zero."}
{"id":"case-394ae9372bce28","assertion":"A says short, independent notes maximize co-presence of particulars so shared structure can be recognized across them.","follow":"B explains conjecture as recognizing particulars as instances of a general structure and identifies recognition as the difficult step.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's use of conjecture and discovery as the benefit of short notes and its evidence that co-loading produces higher-value connections.","reconsider_changed":"If B changed what counts as conjecture or how recognition works, revise A's discovery rationale; if note format or context limits changed, reassess the practical effect.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The composable-notes note asserts that B's particular-to-general recognition process is enabled by co-presence of independently authored notes.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A describes co-loading particulars and shared unnamed structure; B describes conjecture as recognizing such particulars, but the causal bridge is interpretive."}
{"id":"case-92aa92d533a0f1","assertion":"A says links reduce navigation uncertainty per unit of context because every link encounter is a decision about what to read next.","follow":"B states that following any pointer is a probabilistic read-next decision whose cost is reduced by surrounding context.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's candidate theory that link quality is decision-cost reduction and its predictions about titles, typed links, and link density.","reconsider_changed":"If B's navigation model or metadata requirements changed, revise A's explanation and predictions; actual link behavior would require re-evaluation.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The linking-theory note asserts that B's read-next decision is the unit whose uncertainty and context cost its link model measures.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly models links as decisions under bounded context, and B defines that decision and the role of pointer context."}
{"id":"case-41428517ec8382","assertion":"A says retained knowledge is useful only when it can improve future action capacity, not merely when it is stored or retrieved.","follow":"B applies that criterion at the Claw level, distinguishing contextual competence from retrieval and attributing action failures across subsystems.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that discoverability, composability, and trust are a minimal basis for useful memory and that retrieval is insufficient.","reconsider_changed":"If B's action-capacity objective or contribution-attribution boundary changed, revise A's success criterion and surrounding requirements.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The agent-memory note asserts that B's action-capacity criterion is the system-level consequence of useful retained knowledge.","confidence":"high","justification":"A defines usefulness as changed future work under bounded context; B names contextual competence as the broader success criterion and separates it from retrieval."}
{"id":"case-a627c01cfeb3e0","assertion":"A says qualities with weakly discriminating oracles are underselected even when candidates possess those qualities, because accepted outputs become later starting material.","follow":"B generalizes the bottleneck from selection to automation: without cheap discrimination, generation does not become warranted unattended operation.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claims connecting weak quality oracles to autonomy limits and its remedy of stronger external checks; the within-loop selection asymmetry might remain.","reconsider_changed":"If B's automation-verification boundary or oracle-quality caveats changed, revise A's conclusions about warranted autonomy and oracle construction.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The underselection note asserts that B's verification boundary explains why weakly discriminated qualities cannot safely support unattended selection.","confidence":"high","justification":"A distinguishes candidate availability from selection and ties warrant to oracle strength; B makes verification cost the automation boundary without proving A's drift conjecture."}
{"id":"case-cbbd1d7667e81e","assertion":"A says a decomposition's scope is an explanatory-reach claim that must survive refutation-capable use, regardless of whether its boundaries were derived, inherited, or freely chosen.","follow":"B says scale selects against unearned reach rather than explicit structure or human origin, and that automated search does not earn scope without discriminating tests.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's distinction between starting provenance and earned scope, especially its claim that use rather than maturity licenses transfer.","reconsider_changed":"If B's account of scaling or unearned reach changed, revise A's bitter-lesson implication and its requirement for refutation-capable use.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The decomposition-scope note asserts that B's bitter lesson selects on whether claimed reach was tested rather than on whether structure was explicit.","confidence":"high","justification":"A treats scope as explanatory reach earned by refutation-capable use; B makes asserted-versus-tested reach the property scale selects."}
{"id":"case-c34b3568d535fc","assertion":"A says proof-gated self-modification couples evaluation to operative retention, while weakly gated prompt editing makes false acceptances operative.","follow":"B supplies the asymmetry explaining why guaranteed retention concentrates prompt-editing risk at the acceptance gate.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's comparison between proof-gated and prompt-edited systems, especially its claim that prompt-editing risk is concentrated in false-positive acceptance.","reconsider_changed":"If B's filter or retention analysis changed, revise A's risk comparison and empirical-gate recommendation; changes to the prompt harness would alter the retention claim.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The Gödel-machine note asserts that B's false-positive asymmetry explains the prompt-editing corner's exposure when retention is guaranteed.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly contrasts proof-gated retention with prompt edits and invokes operative false acceptance; B defines that exact error path."}
{"id":"case-5996d10a688230","assertion":"A says an enforced tag-README combines a curated map with a machine-checked completeness claim because an agent benefits from the materialized result.","follow":"B explains why materializing a checked completeness result benefits a model reader: recomputation consumes context and can fail, while validation limits staleness.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that the completeness mark is worth adding for an agent and that a machine can cheaply maintain it; the curated map portion is separate.","reconsider_changed":"If B's model-side recompute cost or validation pattern changed, revise A's case for the mark and its maintenance economics.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The enforced-tag-README note asserts that B's recompute-cost inversion makes a validated completeness mark useful to an agent reader.","confidence":"high","justification":"A identifies a machine-rederived membership check and an agent consumer; B states the storage-versus-recompute inversion and safety composition."}
{"id":"case-5ca86f39e5b984","assertion":"A says constraining or extracting an artifact can trade generality for reliability, speed, or cost when the narrowed artifact fits its task.","follow":"B supplies the caution that a deterministic or extracted artifact can be exact for a local requirement while the requirement-to-objective claim remains untested.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's caution that narrowing can improve local execution while failing the larger objective and its recommendation to retain inspectability and fallback.","reconsider_changed":"If B's exactness/proxy distinction or composition test changed, revise A's guidance on when constraining is safe and when extraction should retain fallback material.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The constraining-and-extraction note asserts that B's local-exactness distinction limits what reliability gains from narrowing establish about the larger objective.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A discusses task fit and codification benefits without equating them to objective success; B states that local conformance cannot validate an upstream proxy link."}
{"id":"case-10d4bb9800d9e7","assertion":"A says a proximate target is checked for achievement, while the target-to-objective claim that justifies it remains a separate warrant question.","follow":"B makes the improvement objective a declared, indexed, and causally antecedent parameter, providing the level above the target.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's four-level analysis and its claim that a target-to-objective link is a separate assessable claim.","reconsider_changed":"If B changed how objectives are declared, indexed, or independently specified, revise A's target-oracle separation and composition-failure test.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The proximate-target note asserts that B's declared objective is the higher-level reference separating target achievement from target warrant.","confidence":"high","justification":"A separates target achievement from target-to-objective warrant; B separates the objective's indexed and antecedent roles and warns that properties do not prove their objective."}
{"id":"case-04324ff043d41a","assertion":"A says methodological and computational closure are distinct, with computational closure measured over the pathway's search, evaluation, and retention decisions.","follow":"B defines those three functions and distinguishes completion of the loop from the architecture that performs them.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's profile units and examples for computational closure in proposal-selection pathways; the broader closure distinction would remain.","reconsider_changed":"If B changed what counts as search, evaluation, or operative retention, revise A's per-function allocation profile.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The closure note asserts that B supplies the search, evaluation, and retention functions whose human or computational allocation it measures.","confidence":"high","justification":"A names those exact functions and says the profile is per decision and pathway; B defines them and distinguishes loop completion from architecture."}
{"id":"case-cacf9c28c10bff","assertion":"A says evaluation automation must begin with observed failures, then convert them into calibrated verifiers before broader optimization.","follow":"B provides the operational route from observed behavior and failure clusters to inspectable tests, rules, and checkers.","reconsider_rejected":"Reconsider A's claim that comprehension must precede specification and that verifier construction is a gate before generalization.","reconsider_changed":"If B's mining workflow or codification risks changed, revise A's phase order, automation boundary, and safeguards against accidental regularities.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The evaluation-automation note asserts that B's mining process is the operational route from observed failures to reusable verifiers.","confidence":"high","justification":"A requires observed failures before judges, and B starts from observed behavior or failure clusters and produces inspectable tests and checkers."}

